identifier: kgmicrobe.ingredient:cysteine_hydrochloride_sterile_anoxic_strength_unspecified
preferred_term: Sterile anoxic cysteine hydrochloride preparation (strength unspecified)
mapping_status: MAPPED
ingredient_type: STOCK_SOLUTION
solution_type: OTHER
ontology_mapping:
  ontology_id: kgmicrobe.ingredient:cysteine_hydrochloride_sterile_anoxic_strength_unspecified
  ontology_label: Sterile anoxic cysteine hydrochloride preparation (strength unspecified)
  ontology_source: kgmicrobe.ingredient
  mapping_quality: FALLBACK_REGISTRY
  evidence:
  - evidence_type: LLM_SUGGESTION
    source: https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium375.pdf
    notes: DSMZ375 administers cysteine from a sterile anoxic stock prepared under100%N2.
      Its table specifies source-literal Cystein-HCl x2H2O0.30g as receiving solute
      amount, not stock strength. Solvent, strength, intended two-water form, stereochemistry
      and sterilization method remain unknown; filtration is stated for DTT and vitamins
      only. This is a preparation at the known unspecified-strength scope, not a proven
      chemically disjoint recipe-specific product. It may overlap the DSMZ1107 5%w/v
      preparation, but375 does not establish that concentration or filtration. Existing
      L/monohydrate solutions and W07 scoped stocks do not resolve the unusual stated
      form. No whole-formulation equality, merge or source-number-only disjointness
      is asserted; retain overlap dependency. N2 describes atmosphere, not a material
      component. No exact whole-preparation identity is established by inspected named
      chemical/catalogue owners. Registry scope denotes the preparation, not a pure
      solute or a fully characterized formulation.
